Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 1 year after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 14(1) and 47-2(3) shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation, and the amended provisions of Articles 31-4, 31-5, 59-2, and 62 shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to regional implementation plan for emergency medical services)
The amended provisions of Article 13-3(2) shall begin to apply to the regional implementation plans for emergency medical services formulated after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning National Emergency Medical Center)
The previous duties of the National Emergency Medical Center as at the time this Act enters into force shall be succeeded by the National Emergency Medical Center under the amended provisions of Article 25.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning specialized emergency medical centers)
The National Emergency Medical Center designated as a specialized emergency medical center under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a specialized emergency medical center, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 29(1).
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning regional trauma centers)
The National Emergency Medical Center designated as a regional trauma center under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into shall be deemed a regional trauma center, notwithstanding Article 30-2(1).

