ADDENDA <Act No. 20170, Jan. 30, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 36(2)1, (3)1, and 36-4 shall enter into force 2 years after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability and transitional measures concerning eligibility to take examinations for emergency medical technician paramedics)
(1) The amended provisions of Article 36(2)1 shall begin to apply to persons who enter a university or junior college after the Minister of Health and Welfare publicly announces the designation of a training college for emergency medical technician paramedics under the amended provisions of Article 36-4(3) in the Official Gazette or on the website of the Ministry of Health and Welfare under the amended provisions of Article 36-4(3) after those amended provisions enter into force.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 36(2)1, the previous provisions shall apply to a person who enters a college before the Minister of Health and Welfare publicly announces the designation of a training college for emergency medical technician paramedics under those amended provisions after the amended provisions of Article 36-4(3) enter into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning training institutions for emergency medical technicians)
The Training Institution for Emergency Medical Technicians designated under the previous provisions as at the time the amended provisions of Article 36-4(2) enter into force shall be deemed designated as a training institution for emergency medical technicians under those amended provisions.

