Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force one year after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of the latter part of Article 46(1) shall enter into force 2 years after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to standards for ambulances)
The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 46(1) shall apply beginning with the first ambulance newly registered under Article 8 of the Motor Vehicle Management Act by an operator referred to in Article 44(1)1 after the enforcement of the same amended provisions: provided, in the case of ambulances operated by any of the persons referred to in Article 44(1)2 through 5, the same amended provisions shall apply beginning with the first ambulance newly registered under Article 8 of the Motor Vehicle Management Act after the date three years have elapsed from the date of enforcement of the amended provisions of the latter part of Article 46(1).
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning standards for ambulances)
The previous standards shall apply to an ambulance registered under Article 5 of the Motor Vehicle Management Act in accordance with the previous standards as of the enforcement of the amended provisions of the latter part of Article 46(1), notwithstanding the same amended provisions.

